// #2973: a `{` or `}` inside a string literal nested in an interpolation
// belongs to that literal. The interpolation's brace scan counted it, so
// `"\{"{"}"` was an unterminated string and the `}` case an unlocated
// `unexpected character`.
test "braces inside a nested string literal" {
  inspect("\{"{"}", "{")
  inspect("\{"}"}", "}")
  inspect("a\{String::concat("{", "}")}b", "a{}b")
  inspect("\{String::length("{{}")}", "3")
}
